framework DecisionAudit

domain RetainedReceiptHistory:
  description "Root-cause analysis for GitHub Issue #20"

problem P1:
  "Why does dag history classify an ordinary later task completion as topology_conflict after canonical advance retained a frontier assurance receipt whose producer task was removed?"

step S1:
  premise PR1:
    "Canonical advance may deliberately retain an assurance receipt at the surviving frontier after removing its producer task, so an unchanged receipt and a producer absent from both adjacent snapshots are valid historical state"

step S2:
  evidence EV1:
    "Issue #20 reports a first-parent A to B history in which canonical advance removes A but retains A's frontier assurance receipt for B; the later B completion changes lifecycle, actual evidence, assurance outcome, and acceptance evidence only, yet emits PTHDG-103 topology_conflict"
    resource:
      url "https://github.com/mako10k/perttool/issues/20"
      label "Issue reproduction and expected behavior"

step S3:
  evidence EV2:
    "The current historical transition projector includes every assurance receipt producer_task_id in frozenTaskIds even when the producer task declaration is absent after canonical advance"
    resource:
      file "src/history/historical-transition.ts"
      label "Frozen task inventory"

step S4:
  evidence EV3:
    "frozenTaskPlanChanged looks up every previous frozen task in both adjacent task maps and returns true whenever either lookup is absent, including the stable absent-before and absent-after producer case"
    resource:
      file "src/history/historical-transition.ts"
      label "Frozen plan comparison"

step S5:
  evidence EV4:
    "Immutable assurance records are compared before frozen task planning; a changed or removed retained receipt already fails through immutable conflict or noncanonical removal, so allowing one unchanged receipt's producer to remain absent does not permit receipt mutation"
    resource:
      file "src/history/historical-transition.ts"
      label "Transition classification order"

step S6:
  evidence EV5:
    "The historical transition tests protect changed plan fields for a present frozen task but contain no retained-receipt producer-absence case"
    resource:
      file "test/historical-transition-model.test.mjs"
      label "Existing frozen-task regression boundary"

step S7:
  decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, EV1, EV2, EV3:
    "The root cause is an equality defect in frozen task-plan comparison: legitimate absence from both adjacent snapshots is treated as a plan change because missing identity is collapsed with one-sided disappearance or appearance"

step S8:
  decision D2 based_on PR1, EV3, EV4, D1:
    "The minimal correction treats absent-before and absent-after as equal for one frozen task ID, continues to conflict when exactly one side is absent, and compares endpoints and frozen plan fields when both declarations are present"

step S9:
  decision D3 based_on EV4, EV5, D2:
    "Acceptance must cover an unchanged retained receipt with an absent producer followed by lifecycle and assurance additions, retain conflict for one-sided task presence and changed present frozen task fields, retain immutable receipt conflict, and prove the following canonical advance remains recognized"

step S10:
  decision D4 based_on D1, D2, D3:
    "Historical result identities, Grammar 8, CLI Contract 9, canonical advance proof, assurance meanings, Git evidence bounds, public facades, commands, schemas, adapters, and persistence remain unchanged"

step S11:
  decision D5 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4:
    "The exact owner-confirmed perttool plan was registered, the three-state comparison correction and focused plus real-history regressions were implemented, and the complete repository acceptance gate passed"

step S12:
  pending PD2:
    "Release selection, publication, Issue mutation, plan advance, and unrelated work remain separate boundaries"
